    "body": "Another way to think of this is with a Node.js analogy. `<script type=module src=m.js></script>` is equivalent to `node m.js`. The node binary does not provide any way of getting these top-level module exports. If you want to get them you have to use `require` (`import` in the browser) inside your dependency tree; the top of the dependency tree doesn't use them.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
