    "body": "Yes, the spec is definitely grounded in the historical expectation of how things have always been. We're not interested in catering to novel, unproven module system usages.\r\n\r\nYour example is better rewritten using something like `<reactish-router srcs=\"routeAbout.js routeTwo.js\"></reactish-router>`, as it isn't abusing the `<script type=\"module\">` tag for something it wasn't meant for (importing the top-level modules so they can execute).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
