    "created_at": "2018-10-05T19:06:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-10-05T19:06:33Z",
    "body": "I'd like to re-open this, as I think the underlying \"top-level modules only need to import\" statement is incorrect. The point of exporting from a top-level module would seem to be to make the export visible *to the page's global object* (which is, in a sense, the *true* \"top-level module\"; one that imports all of its inline modules).\r\n\r\nRight now you have to \"fake\" exports from inline modules by explicitly setting `window.foo = ...;` from inside the module; while this *works*, it feels weird to not be able to just export things, and means you can't trivially move a module from inline to external or vice versa.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
