    "updated_at": "2019-08-28T23:22:20Z",
    "body": "One of the main use cases for access to the module object is for declarative custom elements. We talked about a hypothetical `<vue-element>` definition element in Toronto:\r\n\r\nIn an HTML module:\r\n```html\r\n<vue-element name=\"my-element\">\r\n  <template>\r\n    <span v-if=\"isShowing\">I'm shown</span>\r\n  </template>\r\n  <script type=module>\r\n    export default {\r\n      props: ['isShowing'],\r\n      methods: {\r\n        show() {\r\n          this.isShowing = true;\r\n        },\r\n      },\r\n    };\r\n  </script>\r\n</vue-element>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis can work if the `<vue-element>` element can get a reference to the module object created by it's child `<script>` tag.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
